WEBVTT

0
00:00.250 --> 00:01.440
<v Krista>In this video we're talking about</v>

1
00:01.440 --> 00:04.810
multiplication and division of scientific notation together.

2
00:04.810 --> 00:06.390
Notice that we have a fraction here

3
00:06.390 --> 00:08.150
where we have two values in the numerator

4
00:08.150 --> 00:09.390
that are multiplied together

5
00:09.390 --> 00:10.950
and two values in the denominator

6
00:10.950 --> 00:12.180
that are multiplied together.

7
00:12.180 --> 00:13.770
If we look at just the numerator,

8
00:13.770 --> 00:18.040
we have 0.0003 times 10 to the negative six.

9
00:18.040 --> 00:19.910
That's not in scientific notation yet

10
00:19.910 --> 00:21.880
because we have to move the decimal place over

11
00:21.880 --> 00:23.619
until we have 3.0.

12
00:23.619 --> 00:26.270
4000 is also not in scientific notation.

13
00:26.270 --> 00:28.250
So let's start by getting both of the numbers

14
00:28.250 --> 00:30.520
in the numerator in scientific notation

15
00:30.520 --> 00:32.070
before we multiply them together.

16
00:32.070 --> 00:34.033
So for this first value here, .0003,

17
00:35.360 --> 00:37.530
we have to move the decimal to the right

18
00:37.530 --> 00:40.470
one, two, three, four spots

19
00:40.470 --> 00:41.870
until we get it after the three

20
00:41.870 --> 00:43.900
so three can be our whole number.

21
00:43.900 --> 00:46.090
As a result here, we're going to end up with

22
00:46.090 --> 00:49.500
3.0 times, we move the decimal place

23
00:49.500 --> 00:50.820
four places to the right

24
00:50.820 --> 00:52.920
so we're going to get 10 to the negative four,

25
00:52.920 --> 00:54.120
because remember whenever we move

26
00:54.120 --> 00:55.480
the decimal place to the right,

27
00:55.480 --> 00:57.250
the exponent here is going to be negative.

28
00:57.250 --> 00:58.600
So times 10 to the negative four

29
00:58.600 --> 01:00.680
and then times 10 to the negative six,

30
01:00.680 --> 01:01.880
we go head and keep that,

31
01:01.880 --> 01:03.790
and then our 4000 here,

32
01:03.790 --> 01:06.610
we have our decimal place at the end of the 4000.

33
01:06.610 --> 01:08.300
We need to move it to the left until

34
01:08.300 --> 01:09.400
its right after the four,

35
01:09.400 --> 01:12.380
so one, two, three spots,

36
01:12.380 --> 01:14.560
so that's going to leave us with 4.0

37
01:15.590 --> 01:18.160
times 10 to the three,

38
01:18.160 --> 01:19.760
because we moved the decimal place to the left

39
01:19.760 --> 01:21.020
so the exponent is positive

40
01:21.020 --> 01:22.470
and we moved it three spots,

41
01:22.470 --> 01:23.910
we have 10 to the third.

42
01:23.910 --> 01:25.850
Now, we'll simplify by combining this

43
01:25.850 --> 01:26.810
10 to the negative four

44
01:26.810 --> 01:28.170
and 10 to the negative six,

45
01:28.170 --> 01:30.150
we'll have 3.0 times.

46
01:30.150 --> 01:32.430
When we have like bases and we multiply these together,

47
01:32.430 --> 01:33.730
we're going to add the exponents.

48
01:33.730 --> 01:36.490
So negative four plus a negative six is a negative 10,

49
01:36.490 --> 01:38.310
so we get 10 to the negative 10

50
01:38.310 --> 01:41.530
times 4.0 times 10 to the third.

51
01:41.530 --> 01:43.600
Now, when we multiply scientific notation

52
01:43.600 --> 01:44.530
together like this,

53
01:44.530 --> 01:46.240
we deal with the whole numbers together,

54
01:46.240 --> 01:48.760
so we'll do 3.0 times 4.0,

55
01:48.760 --> 01:50.920
is going to be 12.0

56
01:50.920 --> 01:53.510
and then we deal separately with these powers of 10.

57
01:53.510 --> 01:56.770
So 10 to the negative 10 times 10 cubed.

58
01:56.770 --> 01:59.680
Again, we have like bases, so we just add those exponents.

59
01:59.680 --> 02:01.710
Negative 10 plus a positive three

60
02:01.710 --> 02:02.950
is going to be a negative seven,

61
02:02.950 --> 02:05.550
so we get times 10 to the negative seven.

62
02:05.550 --> 02:08.100
And this now is going to be our numerator.

63
02:08.100 --> 02:10.640
So we're just going to leave that alone for a second,

64
02:10.640 --> 02:11.880
that's going to be our numerator.

65
02:11.880 --> 02:13.840
We need to deal now with the denominator

66
02:13.840 --> 02:15.710
before we go head and divide the numerator

67
02:15.710 --> 02:16.720
by the denominator.

68
02:16.720 --> 02:18.550
So looking here at our denominator

69
02:18.550 --> 02:21.240
we need to get this value into scientific notation.

70
02:21.240 --> 02:22.760
We're going to need to move this decimal

71
02:22.760 --> 02:25.240
one, two, three spots to the right

72
02:25.240 --> 02:27.610
so that we end up with 6.0.

73
02:27.610 --> 02:32.610
So here we're going to get 6.0 times 10 to the negative three

74
02:33.230 --> 02:36.430
since we moved the decimal place to the right three spots.

75
02:36.430 --> 02:39.070
And then times 10 to the 15.

76
02:39.070 --> 02:41.490
And then for here, 2000 times 10 to the four,

77
02:41.490 --> 02:43.430
we have our decimal place right here.

78
02:43.430 --> 02:44.880
We need to move it to the left

79
02:44.880 --> 02:48.340
one, two, three spots so it's right after the two

80
02:48.340 --> 02:50.050
and we can call this 2.0.

81
02:50.050 --> 02:54.740
So we're going to say times 2.0 times 10 to the positive

82
02:54.740 --> 02:56.600
one, two, three spots

83
02:56.600 --> 02:58.370
times 10 to the fourth.

84
02:58.370 --> 03:01.340
Now when we simplify here, we'll get 6.0,

85
03:01.340 --> 03:03.700
10 to the negative three times 10 to the 15

86
03:03.700 --> 03:05.640
when you add those exponents together,

87
03:05.640 --> 03:08.140
negative three plus 15 is a positive 12,

88
03:08.140 --> 03:10.280
so we get times 10 to the 12th.

89
03:10.280 --> 03:11.930
And then here we're going to get 2.0

90
03:12.938 --> 03:14.690
10 to the three times 10 to the fourth

91
03:14.690 --> 03:16.150
is going to be 10 to the seventh

92
03:16.150 --> 03:17.750
when we add three and four together,

93
03:17.750 --> 03:19.830
so times 10 to the seventh.

94
03:19.830 --> 03:22.230
And now just like we did for our numerator,

95
03:22.230 --> 03:24.317
we multiply the whole numbers together,

96
03:24.317 --> 03:27.970
6.0 times 2.0 is going to give us 12.0.

97
03:27.970 --> 03:29.870
And then we multiply the powers of 10 together

98
03:29.870 --> 03:32.270
so 10 to the 12 times 10 to the seventh.

99
03:32.270 --> 03:34.080
Again, we add the exponents, so we get

100
03:34.080 --> 03:38.180
times 10 to the 19th, because 12 plus seven is 19.

101
03:38.180 --> 03:41.250
So this then is our denominator.

102
03:41.250 --> 03:43.090
So for our final answer,

103
03:43.090 --> 03:44.420
we're going to take the numerator

104
03:44.420 --> 03:47.740
12.0 times 10 to the negative seven

105
03:47.740 --> 03:49.460
and divide by the denominator

106
03:49.460 --> 03:52.600
12.0 times 10 to the 19

107
03:52.600 --> 03:54.410
and now we just need to simplify

108
03:54.410 --> 03:55.850
by dealing with our whole numbers

109
03:55.850 --> 03:57.480
separately from our powers of 10.

110
03:57.480 --> 04:00.725
So 12.0 divided by 12.0 is going to be

111
04:00.725 --> 04:03.900
1.0 times 10 to the negative seven

112
04:03.900 --> 04:05.330
over 10 to the 19.

113
04:05.330 --> 04:07.420
When we have like bases in a fraction like this,

114
04:07.420 --> 04:09.720
remember we always take the exponent

115
04:09.720 --> 04:11.540
from the numerator, negative seven,

116
04:11.540 --> 04:13.750
and subtract the exponent from the denominator,

117
04:13.750 --> 04:15.500
which in this case is 19.

118
04:15.500 --> 04:18.870
Negative seven minus 19 is a negative 26,

119
04:18.870 --> 04:23.380
so we're going to get 1.0 times 10 to the negative 26

120
04:23.380 --> 04:24.833
for our final answer.